I tried, same behavior. Then I removed the '/App' from the context and specified the entry with /App and it started working (both JS and TS(x)).

Since the output did pick up the change but never the file, should this be a bug? Below my (now working) config:

``` js
var path = require('path');
module.exports = {
    devtool : 'source-map',
    watch: true,
    context: __dirname,
    entry: './App/index',
    output: {
        path: path.join(__dirname, 'wwwroot/dist'),
        filename: '[name]-bundle.js'
    },
    resolve: {
        extensions: ['', '.js', '.ts', '.tsx', '.css'],        
    },
    module: {
        loaders: [
            { test: /\.tsx?$/, loaders: ['ts-loader']},
            { test: /\.css$/, loader: 'style-loader'}
        ]
    },
    plugins: []
}
```

